pi.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If the other streams have the same order, that's probably fine.\n\nI checked the code: the wav player is from 2017, the other two from 2020 and 2021. It's likely that back when writing the wav player, the possibility to abort a seek was simply not considered.\n\nThe only alternative I can see is replacing `start()` to return a boolean. That might be a good idea anyhow, since `AudioStreamPlaybackWAV` is doing a bunch of stuff after seek. But that would mean a change in API — seek seems currently not allowed to abort at all (wild!), so maybe we should discuss this change first before doing it.","created_at":"2026-05-22T08:25:29Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T08:25:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119446#discussion_r3287003124","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119446","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3287003124"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119446#discussion_r3287003124"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119446"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3287003124/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}